        "title": "refactor(deadcode): trim mid-size src exports",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe production Knip unused-export ratchet still carried hundreds of dead internal exports across mid-size `src` areas. Test-only references kept some internal symbols looking useful even though production-mode Knip correctly classified them as dead.\n\nRelated: #105595\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Removes or localizes dead exports in `src/auto-reply`, `src/commands`, `src/cli`, `src/secrets`, `src/cron`, `src/tasks`, and the unowned `src/*` tail.\n- Keeps documented CLI commands and flags unchanged; setup/onboard help remains intact.\n- Redirects tests through production owner seams or explicit test helpers where the deleted symbol was test-only.\n- Leaves sibling-owned agents, plugins, infra, config, gateway, and channels baseline burn-downs out of scope.\n- Regenerates the enforced production Knip baseline as a 662-entry removal-only shrink (4,959 entries remain).\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intended runtime or CLI behavior change. The codebase exposes fewer internal symbols, carries less dead code, and lowers the unused-export baseline for subsequent ratcheted cleanups.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports:update` + `pnpm deadcode:exports` (4,959 exact match)\n- Plugin SDK API/package/export guards and core/core-test/extension `tsgo`\n- `pnpm build`\n- 2,632 focused tests across auto-reply, commands, CLI, cron, secrets, and tasks\n- 424 focused process/session/gateway/Plugin SDK tests\n- 182 focused pairing/migration/doctor tests\n- `pnpm check:changed` (full changed gate, 12m33s)\n- root, setup, onboard, and configure CLI help smoke checks\n- fresh Codex autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings\n\nTestbox evidence: [focused + deadcode](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29218372933), [pairing tail](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29219209158).\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n",
